comments.body:
@participant6:
Yes, the `sense` integration absolutely needs to set the `last_reset` property for energy sensors that reset daily, monthly etc.
We should try to get a fix in a patch release before the end of the year 👍

The actual value of `last_reset` is not at all important, what's important is that it changes **together with the 1st value of a new cycle**, it's explained here how it works: https://developers.home-assistant.io/docs/core/entity/sensor#state-class-total

@participant12 summarized like this for state class `total` sensors:
> the logic behind the statistics table is to update the sum column with the difference between the current state and the previous state unless last_reset has been changed, in which case don't add anything

@participant6 if the sense API updates only hourly, you can consider using the API for injecting external statistics instead of injecting it via a sensor. that will also allow you to import and correct historical data. 
here's an example of how it can be implemented: <https://github.com/home-assistant/core/pull/62249>

tibber is a bit different though since you get details of the past day after midnight, in this case it probably doesn't matter that the values are off by an hour
